WEBVTT

00:00.140 --> 00:01.520
Look at this sentence:

00:01.820 --> 00:04.390
“The number of users went up a lot

00:04.690 --> 00:07.240
between 2010 and 2020.”

00:07.540 --> 00:09.930
It's not wrong, but it wouldn't get a high score.

00:10.230 --> 00:10.694
Why not?

00:10.694 --> 00:12.910
Well, let's make it stronger in four steps.

00:13.210 --> 00:15.790
So, building the sentence. First of all,

00:16.090 --> 00:18.580
the verb. “Went up” is informal,

00:18.880 --> 00:20.460
so it becomes “rose”.

00:20.760 --> 00:22.257
Secondly, the adverb.

00:22.257 --> 00:25.659
“A lot” doesn't tell the reader very much at all.

00:25.659 --> 00:27.360
It doesn't tell us a lot.

00:27.660 --> 00:30.351
The number went from 2 million to 9 million,

00:30.351 --> 00:32.026
so it more than quadrupled.

00:32.026 --> 00:33.640
That's quite a big change,

00:33.640 --> 00:36.810
so “rose dramatically” would be a better choice here.

00:37.110 --> 00:39.250
Thirdly, the figures.

00:39.550 --> 00:42.705
Add the start and the end, with units:

00:42.705 --> 00:44.970
from 2 million to 9 million.

00:45.270 --> 00:46.140
And fourth,

00:46.550 --> 00:47.240
the time.

00:47.640 --> 00:51.390
Keep the period clear: between 2010 and 2020.

00:51.690 --> 00:52.867
So now we have:

00:52.867 --> 00:55.808
“The number of users rose dramatically,

00:55.808 --> 00:58.529
climbing from 2 million to 9 million

00:58.529 --> 01:00.220
between 2010 and 2020.”

01:00.520 --> 01:03.314
The verb has to match the shape of the line.

01:03.314 --> 01:06.294
If sales rose slowly and steadily for 10 years,

01:06.294 --> 01:07.660
they climbed steadily.

01:07.960 --> 01:10.274
“Surged” or “soared” would be wrong,

01:10.274 --> 01:12.900
because those describe a sudden, big jump.

01:13.200 --> 01:17.458
Watch out for verbs that carry feelings and connotation.

01:17.458 --> 01:20.520
“Boomed” and “flourished” sound positive.

01:20.820 --> 01:22.590
“Spiralled” sounds out of control.

01:22.890 --> 01:26.150
You wouldn't say pollution flourished, or

01:26.450 --> 01:30.474
illiteracy boomed, because these are negative things,

01:30.474 --> 01:33.901
pollution and illiteracy. These are not good.

01:33.901 --> 01:36.583
So “boom” is usually used for sales

01:36.583 --> 01:40.682
or something more positive. So you might use it there.

01:40.682 --> 01:43.960
So be careful with the connotation of words.

01:44.260 --> 01:47.881
As an examiner, I wouldn't reward the most dramatic words.

01:47.881 --> 01:50.274
I would reward the most accurate ones.

01:50.274 --> 01:51.870
Keep Task 1 quite neutral

01:51.870 --> 01:54.079
and let the numbers do the talking.

01:54.079 --> 01:57.147
Your comparison is also very important in Task 1.

01:57.147 --> 01:58.620
Don't forget to compare.

01:58.920 --> 02:01.212
Now, try the five rounds on the right.

02:01.212 --> 02:03.092
The first three test precision,

02:03.092 --> 02:05.090
and the last two test connotation.
